[medium] Possible memory leak here: `PyMem_Free(filename)` only executes if `FemVTKTools::frdToVTK()` returns normally. If that call throws — for example a `Base::FileException` because the file is unreadable — the buffer allocated by `PyArg_ParseTuple` for 'filename' is never released. This breaks the RAII principle. Consider an RAII wrapper, or free the buffer before the function call instead.

```suggestion
        if (!PyArg_ParseTuple(args.ptr(), "et", "utf-8", &filename)) {
            throw Py::Exception();
        }
        std::string encodedName = std::string(filename);
        PyMem_Free(filename);

        try {
            FemVTKTools::frdToVTK(encodedName.c_str());
        } catch (const Base::Exception& e) {
            throw Py::RuntimeError(e.what());
        }
```
